<Layouts.app flash={@flash} current_scope={@current_scope} mode="marketing">
  <div class="walkthrough">
    <header class="walkthrough-intro">
      <.link href={~p"/"} class="ui-link inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm">
        <.icon name="hero-arrow-left" class="size-4" /> Back to home
      </.link>
      <h1 id="how-it-works-title">How OneSQLx works.</h1>
      <p>
        Start with a PostgreSQL connection. Follow a question with SQL.
        Turn the answer into something your team can use.
      </p>
    </header>

    <ol id="walkthrough-steps" class="walkthrough-steps">
      <li class="walkthrough-step">
        <div class="walkthrough-step-title">
          <span class="walkthrough-step-number" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
          <h2>Connect your data.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="walkthrough-step-body">
          <p>
            In <strong>Data Sources</strong>, add a PostgreSQL source with its host,
            port, database name, and credentials. Enable SSL if your database requires it;
            keep read-only mode enabled for analytical work.
          </p>
          <p>
            Open its catalog to explore schemas, tables, and columns before writing your first query.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="walkthrough-step">
        <div class="walkthrough-step-title">
          <span class="walkthrough-step-number" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
          <h2>Ask with SQL.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="walkthrough-step-body">
          <p>
            Open the <strong>SQL Editor</strong>, select your data source, and write a query.
            Use schema-aware autocomplete, run it, and inspect the results below the editor.
          </p>
          <div class="walkthrough-example">
            <p>Example query · replace <code>your_table</code> with a table from your catalog.</p>
            <pre><code>SELECT COUNT(*) AS total_rows
FROM your_table;</code></pre>
          </div>
          <p>
            Save the query with a title to reuse it in a dashboard, or export its results
            as CSV, JSON, or Excel.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="walkthrough-step">
        <div class="walkthrough-step-title">
          <span class="walkthrough-step-number" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
          <h2>Share the insight.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="walkthrough-step-body">
          <p>
            In <strong>Dashboards</strong>, create a dashboard and add a card using your saved
            query. Choose a visualization that fits the result, then arrange it alongside
            the other questions your team follows.
          </p>
          <p>
            Work together in your workspace, or generate a read-only sharing link when
            you want to make a dashboard available without a login.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <section class="walkthrough-start" aria-labelledby="walkthrough-start-title">
      <div>
        <h2 id="walkthrough-start-title">Bring your first question.</h2>
        <p>Open your workspace and start exploring your data.</p>
      </div>
      <.link
        id="walkthrough-start"
        href={if(@current_scope, do: ~p"/sql-editor", else: ~p"/users/register")}
        class="ui-button ui-button-primary"
      >
        {if(@current_scope, do: "Open your workspace", else: "Start exploring")}
        <.icon name="hero-arrow-up-right" class="size-4" />
      </.link>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layouts.app>
